---
// The brand-story section — explains the name and ties the bird imagery to
// the actual product idea instead of using it as pure decoration.
---

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center reveal">
  <div class="md:col-span-6 relative">
    <div class="paper-pinned p-3 -rotate-2 relative">
      <div class="tape -top-3 left-10 -rotate-3"></div>
      <img
        src="/images/flock-circle.png"
        alt="A small circle of birds gathered together, facing one another"
        class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-cover"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="absolute -bottom-6 -right-4 vellum-panel p-4 w-40 rotate-3 hidden sm:block">
      <div class="eyebrow mb-1">Noun</div>
      <p class="font-serif text-sm text-ink leading-snug">
        A small group of birds, gathered and moving as one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="md:col-span-6">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-3">Why "Covey"</div>
    <h2 class="display text-4xl md:text-5xl mb-6 text-balance">
      Birds don't flock in <span class="italic text-clay">crowds</span>.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-warm-gray leading-relaxed text-lg mb-5">
      A covey is a small gathering of quail — ten or fifteen birds, never a
      hundred. They move together, watch out for each other, and scatter
      back to their own lives when the day is done.
    </p>
    <p class="text-warm-gray leading-relaxed text-lg">
      That's the whole app in one word. Not a crowd, not a feed — a small
      group of people, gathered around one plan, for one day.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
